KONOHAGAKURE — CHUNIN SELECTION EXAM ELIGIBILITY

The Chunin Selection Exams assess whether a genin is ready to lead and to make command decisions in the field.

Eligibility:
- A genin must be nominated by their jonin-sensei.
- Nomination is by full three-member cell; the team enters together.
- Sufficient mission experience is expected before nomination, though sensei discretion governs.
- Foreign genin from allied and participating villages may enter the host village's exam under inter-village agreement.

The exam is held in stages (information gathering, survival, and individual combat) and tests intelligence, endurance, and judgment, not merely combat victory. Promotion to Chunin is decided by observing judges based on chunin-level qualities displayed, and confirmed by the Hokage — a candidate may be promoted without winning the final tournament.
Issued by the Chunin Exam administration.
